Myth: **The Moon's Promise**

Before the world knew rhythm, the Moon wandered aimlessly across the heavens, uncertain and dim. She envied the Sun's purpose—to bring light and mark the days. "What am I for?" she asked the stars, but they only twinkled wordlessly.

One night, the Moon descended to Earth and met the Ocean, who was equally troubled. "I have no direction," the Ocean confessed. "I spread everywhere and nowhere, without shape or meaning."

The Moon understood this loneliness. "Let us help each other," she proposed. "I will pull you toward me, giving you motion and purpose. In return, your rising waters will reflect my light, making me visible and beautiful."

