The starfish looked at her curled companion. "If we both believe the other gives nothing... we both curl up. We both starve. Both certain the other betrayed us."

The elders whisper: Sometimes the reef isn't barren and the fish aren't cruel. Sometimes the water itself is lying. But how do you reach out when you can't trust what you see?

